{
  "id": 337803589,
  "iid": 17834,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "epan: Fix asn1 REAL number decoding",
  "description": "MR provides two fixes:\n\n1. Adjusted the assertion from `lenE < len - 1` to `lenE < len` because `len` is decremented after decoding info_octet.\n\nNote that `len = 1B (info_octet) + lenE (Exponent Length, 1-3B) + lenM (Mantissa Length)`.\n\nSpecifically, the `len` value includes the following bytes: \n- 1Byte info_octet\n- 1-3 Bytes Exponent Length (`lenE = (info_octet & 0x3) + 1`)\n- (`len - lenE - 1`) Bytes mantissa.\n\nIndeed, the `lenE < len - 1`. However, `len` is decremented after decoding info_octet [here](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/epan/asn1.c?ref_type=heads#L198-L200)\n\n2. Removed the incorrect check that treated (`val_length == 0`) as an unexpected length, allowing proper decoding of REAL numbers with zero length. The length zero is valid for ASN.1 REAL types representing the value `0.0`.\n\nWith the MR, Real numbers are correctly decoded:\n\n![image](/uploads/6df0b8adefe82b4ed3536668c221f9b8/image.png)",
